WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
<v Clara Vogel>Thanks for making time. Two items today: the T2 launch and cash. Mia, you go first on cash.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
<v Mia Janssen>Cash is at EUR 7.9M at the end of September. Q3 revenue came in at EUR 3.4M, so we are safe for the next two quarters, but the battery orders for T2 need a clear plan.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Clara Vogel>Agreed. Let's keep the battery plan on the agenda for the November meeting.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Niklas Roth>On dealers: we have 62 in DE, NL and BE. The strategy memo has us doubling the network in Germany and the Netherlands, so I want the dealer pipeline in front of us each month.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
<v Mia Janssen>Good. Can the pipeline show onboarding status as well as signed dealers?

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:45.000
<v Clara Vogel>Yes. Now the T2 launch. I am setting the launch of the Model T2 for 15 March 2027, and this date is final.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
<v Mia Janssen>We will plan the team calendar around the 15 March 2027 launch.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
<v Niklas Roth>That gives marketing about five months for the teaser. Lea will need the campaign shape before the end of the year.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Clara Vogel>Agreed. We will write the teaser budget into the decisions note once Jonas has checked the numbers.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:12.000
<v Mia Janssen>Engineering says build 3 of the prototype is on track. Tobias will confirm that in writing this week.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:19.000
<v Niklas Roth>Good. Then the calendar work can start. I will draft the milestones for the product team and send them to Priya.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:26.000
<v Clara Vogel>Please keep the milestones at the level of weeks, not days. The team needs room to move.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:33.000
<v Mia Janssen>Understood. I will also add the all-hands on 30 October to the shared calendar, so that everyone has the date.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:40.000
<v Niklas Roth>On Amsterdam, sales is steady. Daan's pipeline is strong, and Sanne has the dealer contacts in order.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:47.000
<v Clara Vogel>Good to hear. Let's keep an eye on the margin, though. We want to hold the 38% gross margin on T1 while volume grows.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:54.000
<v Mia Janssen>Jonas is building the margin model for that. He will have a first version before the November meeting.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:01.000
<v Niklas Roth>Then I think we have what we need on dealers and margin. Anything else on cash?

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:08.000
<v Clara Vogel>Only that we keep the reserve as it is. No new commitments until the November review.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.000
<v Mia Janssen>Noted. I will put that in the notes and send them within one working day, as usual.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.000
<v Clara Vogel>Good. Each decision today goes into the decisions note with the date and an owner. Thanks, everyone.
